ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The American Cancer Society Cancer Prevention Study-3 (CPS-3) is a prospective cohort study of over 300,000 US adults with the primary goal of investigating cancer incidence and mortality") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11329134/fullTextXML") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "cancer") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_population_study_of obo:MONDO_0004992) coho:COHO_0002685)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The focus of research work has been on the incidence of infectious diseases in children, defining risk factors including genetic risks, and interventions to prevent infectious diseases—particularly vaccines.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3396317/fullTextXML") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "infectious disease") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_population_study_of obo:MONDO_0005550) coho:COHO_0002689)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Cancer Prevention Study II Nutrition Cohort was established in 1992 and was designed to investigate the relation between diet and other lifestyle factors and exposures and the risk of cancer, mortality, and survival.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12015775+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "cancer") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_population_study_of obo:MONDO_0004992) coho:COHO_0002690)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The pilot is the first large-scale population-based screening project in China aimed at identifying subjects at high risk of cardiovascular disease (CVD) and collecting detailed information and biospecimens as part of a precision medicine project.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4716208/fullTextXML") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "cardiovascular disease") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_population_study_of obo:MONDO_0004995) coho:COHO_0002693)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The aim of ACDIS was to describe the demographic, social and health impacts of a rapidly progressing HIV epidemic in rural South Africa, and to monitor the impact of intervention strategies.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7938501/fullTextXML") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "HIV") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_population_study_of obo:MONDO_0005109) coho:COHO_0002694)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Funded by an NMRC OF-LCG grant that brought together four longitudinal cohorts in Singapore, the SG100K cohort is an Investigator-Initiated Study focused on determinants and prediction of cardiovascular disease and diabetes in Asian populations.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.npm.sg/our-data-users/data-access/data-access-to-precise-sg100k/") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "cardiovascular disease") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_population_study_of obo:MONDO_0004995) coho:COHO_0002696)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Funded by an NMRC OF-LCG grant that brought together four longitudinal cohorts in Singapore, the SG100K cohort is an Investigator-Initiated Study focused on determinants and prediction of cardiovascular disease and diabetes in Asian populations.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.npm.sg/our-data-users/data-access/data-access-to-precise-sg100k/") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "diabetes") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_population_study_of obo:MONDO_0005015) coho:COHO_0002696)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Inclusion criteria were; documented acute coronary syndrome (myocardial infarction or unstable angina) confirmed on coronary angiogram; and age ≤ 50 years for males or ≤ 55 years for females.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1289285/fullTextXML") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "acute coronary syndrome") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_patients_with obo:MONDO_0005542) coho:COHO_0002702)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "It aimed at improving fat quality and promoting healthy foods to prevent cardiovascular diseases.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13092225/fullTextXML") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "cardiovascular disease") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:is_population_study_of obo:MONDO_0004995) coho:COHO_0002703)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "In short, AF RISK was a multicenter, prospective, observational study, including patients aged ≥ 18 years, with pAF (total AF history < 2 years, or total AF history < 3 years in case of ≤ 2 AF episodes of ≤ 48 h per month terminating spontaneously) or persistent AF (total AF history < 2 years, and total persistent AF duration > 7 days and < 1 year) in whom a rhythm control strategy was preferred.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8914333/fullTextXML") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "atrial fibrillation") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_patients_with obo:MONDO_0004981) coho:COHO_0002704)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "At the outpatient clinic patients with AF onset <60 years, ≥18 years at time of inclusion were asked to participate.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6923497/fullTextXML") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "atrial fibrillation") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_patients_with obo:MONDO_0004981) coho:COHO_0002705)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Biomarker AF study (ClinicalTrials.gov Identifier: NCT01510197) is an observational hospital-based cohort (n=500; in GGAF 458) to identify a risk profile to guide AF therapy in all-comers with AF.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0133-9/MediaObjects/41588_2018_133_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "atrial fibrillation") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_patients_with obo:MONDO_0004981) coho:COHO_0002706)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To evaluate the effect of metformin treatment on preservation of left ventricular function in patients without diabetes presenting with ST-segment elevation myocardial infarction (STEMI).") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24687169+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "ST-segment elevation myocardial infarction") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_patients_with obo:MONDO_0041656) coho:COHO_0002707)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Colorectal cancer (CRC) cases for the project were derived from the Shanghai Women’s Health Study (SWHS) and the Shanghai Men’s Health Study (SMHS), both population-based cohort studies which are being conducted in urban Shanghai, China.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2505/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2505_MOESM12_ESM.pdf") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "colorectal cancer") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_patients_with obo:MONDO_0005575) coho:COHO_0002708)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The HCES is a hospital-based case-control study conducted in South Korea that includes multiple cancers 13, 14 .") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2985/MediaObjects/41588_2014_BFng2985_MOESM57_ESM.pdf") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "cancer") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_patients_with obo:MONDO_0004992) coho:COHO_0002709)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the present study DNA was available from a total of 2126 prostate cancer cases and 2403 unaffected men.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2560/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2560_MOESM4_ESM.pdf") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "prostate cancer") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_patients_with obo:MONDO_0008315) coho:COHO_0002710)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Childhood Cancer and Leukemia International Consortium (CLIC) was established in 2007 to study the etiology of childhood leukemia and later expanded in 2019 to include other childhood cancers, principally solid tumors.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13544941/") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "childhood cancers") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_patients_with obo:MONDO_0006517) coho:COHO_0002711)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Australian Study of Causes of Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia in Children (Aus-ALL) was designed to test the hypothesis, raised by a previous Western Australian study, that maternal folic acid supplementation during pregnancy might reduce the risk of childhood acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL).") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19839053+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "childhood acute lymphoblastic leukemia") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_patients_with obo:MONDO_0000870) coho:COHO_0002712)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "InterLymph was established in 2000 as a voluntary consortium that facilitates collaboration among epidemiologic studies of lymphoma (http://epi.grants.cancer.gov/InterLymph).") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1852242/") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "lymphoma") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_patients_with obo:MONDO_0005062) coho:COHO_0002713)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "We randomly assigned 1370 patients with newly diagnosed early-stage Hodgkin's lymphoma with a favorable prognosis to one of four treatment groups") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20818855+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "Hodgkin's lymphoma") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_patients_with obo:MONDO_0004952) coho:COHO_0002714)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients age 16 to 75 years with newly diagnosed early unfavorable HL were randomly assigned in a 2 × 2 factorial design") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20713848+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "Hodgkin's lymphoma") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_patients_with obo:MONDO_0004952) coho:COHO_0002715)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "In HD12 (Jan 4, 1999, to Jan 13, 2003; registered with ClinicalTrials.gov [NCT00265031]), 1670 patients with newly diagnosed, histology-proven, advanced-stage Hodgkin's lymphoma received eight cycles of eBEACOPP or four cycles of eBEACOPP plus four cycles of bBEACOPP (4 + 4), plus consolidation radiotherapy to initial bulk and residual disease or no radiotherapy, to analyse two non-inferiority objectives.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30290903+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "Hodgkin's lymphoma") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_patients_with obo:MONDO_0004952) coho:COHO_0002716)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Specifically, we report findings on the associations between bladder cancer risk and each SNP and their interactions with cigarette smoking.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2782435/") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "bladder cancer") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_patients_with obo:MONDO_0001187) coho:COHO_0002717)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases were all new incident breast cancer patients histologically diagnosed at the National Cancer Institute in Bangkok and at the hospital in Khon Kaen province of North Eastern of Thailand during the period of May 2002 to March 2004 [21], with a participation rate of 99.6% (554/556).") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10549-007-9773-7") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "breast cancer") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_patients_with obo:MONDO_0007254) coho:COHO_0002718)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "To examine the genetic factors underlying familial glioma, the Genetic Epidemiology of Glioma International Consortium (GLIOGENE Consortium) was formed in 2006 to recruit families affected by ≥2 cases of glioma from 14 institutions across 5 countries (12).") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4706682/") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "glioma") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_patients_with obo:MONDO_0021042) coho:COHO_0002720)
ClassAssertion(Annotation(rdfs:comment "We enrolled 782 patients through hospitals in Phoenix, Arizona; Boston; and Pittsburgh; 489 had histologically confirmed glioma, 197 had meningioma, and 96 had acoustic neuroma. The 799 controls were patients admitted to the same hospitals as the patients with brain tumors for a variety of nonmalignant conditions.") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi?db=pubmed&id=11150357&retmode=xml") Annotation(obo:IAO_0000116 "acoustic neuroma") ObjectSomeValuesFrom(coho:has_patients_with obo:MONDO_0001569) coho:COHO_0002721)
